{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvyVm1FkRqUAk5GqDqPM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JKPHiWeXEPLio75JG63mde","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\na=s.index(\"\\\\[\\n\\\\hat y\")\nb=s.index(\"\\\\]\",a)+2\nnew=\"\"\"\\\\[\n\\\\hat y_{\\\\text{plain}} = \\\\frac1n\\\\Big(\\\\sum_{i\\\\in\\\\mathcal I} Y_i+\\\\sum_{i\\\\notin\\\\mathcal I}\\\\hat p_i\\\\Big),\\\\qquad\n\\\\hat y_{\\\\text{corr}} = \\\\hat y_{\\\\text{plain}} + \\\\frac{n-k}{n}\\\\,\\\\overline{(Y-\\\\hat p)_{\\\\mathcal I}},\n\\\\]\"\"\"\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"The model-assisted estimate is\\n\",\"The model-assisted estimate, with and without a residual correction, is\\n\")\ns=s.replace(\"where $\\\\hat p_i$ is the model probability.\",\"where $\\\\hat p_i$ is the model probability and the correction adds the mean residual of the revealed items, extrapolated to the unrevealed items.\")\nadd=\"\"\"\\\\paragraph{Practical reading.} For a user who only needs coarse model scores on benchmarks resembling the historical pool, the random-target numbers (MAE 0.0179, Spearman 0.956 at $k=100$) indicate that 100 items can recover full accuracy to within about two percentage points on average and keep rankings largely intact. % @evidence[[derived/metrics_summary.json#final.mae_random_targets]]\nFor a user who must rank systems that exceed everything in the historical pool, the strong-target numbers (MAE 0.0409, Spearman 0.730) indicate that subset predictions alone should be treated as screening information, with direct evaluation reserved for the decisions that matter. Whether the stacked configuration or a plain random-subset mean is preferable for this purpose cannot be decided from our evidence, because their difference is smaller than the uncertainty we measured; the random mean is simpler, needs no source data, and has no regime-dependent tuning.\n\n\\\\paragraph{Relation to published numbers.} We do not compare against numbers reported in earlier papers: protocols differ in benchmark sets, target definitions, item budgets and metrics, and our baselines are re-implementations with fixed settings rather than the original code. Conclusions here are limited to the matched comparison on the evaluator's episodes.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"\\\\paragraph{Not tested.}\",add+\"\\\\paragraph{Not tested.}\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"Practical reading\" paper.tex | head -2\n(pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l1.log 2>&1; bibtex paper >/tmp/b.log 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l2.log 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l3.log 2>&1); grep -E \"Overfull|Error|undefined\" /tmp/l3.log | head; $TMPDIR/pyenv/bin/python - <<'E'\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\nimport re\nr=PdfReader('paper.pdf'); print(len(r.pages))\nfor i in range(6,9):\n    t=re.sub(r'\\n\\d{3}\\n',' ',r.pages[i].extract_text()); print(i+1,len(t.split()),t[-120:].replace('\\n',' '))\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1323,"cache_read_input_tokens":173375,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1323},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"04560f3a-5349-4633-b910-06f62141dcd0","uuid":"3dcedbe1-028d-4066-9c8a-624030affc2b","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:22:28.425Z","request_id":"req_011CgvyVjKo6zsqzMRn2Facd"}
