{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvyYqjM2s2M8vzLv9y81","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AJw9x3FJktZRaCKXVaSspT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('paper.tex').read()\nadd=\"\"\"\\\\paragraph{What would resolve the comparison.} The width of the MAE-gain interval (0.0186) is about four times its point estimate (0.0045), so the held-out panel is too small to distinguish a gain of this size from zero. A decisive test would need more benchmarks and seeds than the five and three used here, paired in the same way, together with per-regime baseline results so that any gain can be located in the in-range or out-of-range regime. We expect, but have not verified, that the sign of the gain is more stable than its magnitude.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s.replace(\"\\\\paragraph{Not tested.}\",add+\"\\\\paragraph{Not tested.}\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(s)\nE\n(pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l1.log 2>&1; bibtex paper >/tmp/b.log 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l2.log 2>&1; pdflatex -interaction=nonstopmode paper.tex >/tmp/l3.log 2>&1); $TMPDIR/pyenv/bin/python - 2>/dev/null <<'E'\nimport fitz\nd=fitz.open('paper.pdf'); print(len(d))\nfor i in (7,8):\n    p=d[i]; ys=[b[3] for b in p.get_text('blocks') if b[4].strip() and not b[4].strip().isdigit() and 'Generated by' not in b[4] and b[0]>80]\n    print(i+1,max(ys), p.get_text()[:60].replace('\\n',' '))\nd[7].get_pixmap(dpi=60).save('/tmp/p8.png'); d[0].get_pixmap(dpi=60).save('/tmp/p1.png')\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":697,"cache_read_input_tokens":176816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":697},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transf